  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat a large skillet over medium-high heat.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Once the skillet is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add beef, salt, and pepper; cook, breaking the meat apart with a spoon, until browned and crumbly, 4-5 minutes.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 tsp extra virgin olive oil\n1 lb lean ground beef\n½ tsp salt\n¼ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, finely chop half of the pickles and place in a small bowl. Add mayo, ketchup, and vinegar, then stir to combine the special sauce; set aside. (Reserve remaining pickles for later use.)\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ cup dill pickle chips\n½ cup mayonnaise\n2 tbsp ketchup\n1 tsp white vinegar"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the beef is done, remove from heat. Add ketchup, mustard, and Worcestershire to the skillet, then stir to combine the filling. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "ketchup\n1 tsp yellow mustard\n½ tsp Worcestershire sauce"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "To assemble the quesadillas, lay tortillas on a flat surface and divide filling between them, arranging on one half of each tortilla. Top with remaining pickles and shredded cheese, then fold in half to close.",
      "secondary_message": "1 ½ cups cheddar cheese, shredded"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Wipe the skillet clean with paper towels and return to medium-high heat; add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Working in batches, place assembled quesadillas in the skillet and cook, flipping halfway through, until tortillas are golden on both sides, 5-6 minutes. Remove to a plate.\n\n\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "extra virgin olive oil"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Cut each quesadilla into wedges and divide between plates. Serve with special sauce for dipping and enjoy!\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
